    "biography": {
      "en": "Muhammad Nasrul Mohamed Noor is a certified Disability Equality Training (DET) Facilitator, disability inclusion advocate, and researcher dedicated to advancing the rights and inclusion of persons with disabilities. His work focuses on disability equality, accessibility, psychosocial disabilities, inclusive public transport, and universal design. He is committed to promoting evidence-based practices and leveraging technology to create accessible, inclusive, and equitable communities.",

      "ms": "Muhammad Nasrul Mohamed Noor ialah Fasilitator Latihan Kesaksamaan OKU (DET) bertauliah, penyokong keterangkuman OKU dan penyelidik yang komited memperjuangkan hak serta penyertaan orang kurang upaya. Bidang tumpuannya merangkumi kesaksamaan OKU, kebolehcapaian, ketidakupayaan psikososial, pengangkutan awam inklusif dan reka bentuk sejagat."
    }
  },

